      "affected_surface": "Plan §6 card disposition summary plus §7 successor guided-compatibility baseline design; downstream P4 migration machinery and P7 swap commit",
      "claim": "The successor-baseline ontology has only two outcomes (verbatim relocation into the extended references/ universe, or explicit removed dispositions for truly deleted duplicates), but §6 also commits to KEEP-compressed transformations that are neither, so the P7 swap either fails its own superset gate or silently exempts reworded content from the relocation-not-loss proof.",
      "evidence": "§7 itself states the constraint byte-level: deleting or rewording ANY of the pinned lines triggers PROFILE_GUIDED_COMPATIBILITY_DRIFT, and the immutable P0 snapshot covers 661 of the current 713 lines, so the compression targets (Phase-1 session-start prose, scope-creep indicators converted to a table, L-1 intent, L-4 per-phase, anti-patterns table with row trims) are almost certainly inside the required multiset; §6 marks only the S Session End CUT as requiring P4 and assigns no disposition class to compressed or trimmed rows, leaving the dominant-risk verification unable to either pass or prove anything about transformed content.",
      "evidence_reference": "PLAN_UNDER_REVIEW_d5a8664ce38e45133ddaf201 §6 KEEP-compressed list and CUT note; §7 Approach paragraph ('Deleting or rewording ANY of those lines', 'Truly deleted duplicates get explicit removed dispositions')",
